     <h1 class="title" title="Wayanad Hill Station">Wayanad</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/Wayanad-hill-station.jpg" title="Wayanad hill station" alt="Wayanad hill station, hill stations in india, South india hill stations, Wayanad" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Kerala<br />
<b>Area:</b> 89 sq.kms<br />
<b>Significance: Land of  Paddy Fields</b> <br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2132m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 26&#176;C to 32&#176;C, Winter 15&#176;C to 20&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> September to May</p>
<p>Wayanad the green paradise surrounded by mountains from the <b>Western Ghats</b>, which form part of the world the green <b>border of Kerala</b>. Pure and pristine, enchanting and hypnotizing, this land steeped in history and culture. Located at a distance of 76 km. <b>Kozhikode Sea coast</b>, this resort green hill surrounded by orchards, forests and wildlife. <b>Wayanad hills</b> linked Mudumalai in <b>Tamil Nadu</b> and Karnataka Bandhipur, thus forming a large mass of land for wildlife to move in their most natural home.
</p>





